                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Good concept in theory, if the devs weren't complete dogshiit. \n\nThis game always has been, and likely always will be carried by the community that plays it, not the devs, they are worthless and most just money grubbers. These devs are the epitome of devs too prideful to listen to the community until it's way too late. I can't say they never listen to the community's sentiments, they do listen, but only after they try and fail at everything else, it takes them YEARS to go back on decisions that nobody asks for, YEARS to implement simple QoL changes that have been asked for since day one, YEARS to consider maybe the dedicated community of competitive level players might know more about the game than some devs who can't even break past diamond ranks on their own. \n\nAnd that's the exact biggest issue with this game, even if the devs play, none of them play at a high enough level to understand what it's actually like at the top or why people play. The strategy of this game has been completely hollowed out to be honest, this game used to be like a sort rock-paper-scissors with a lot of nuance in the strategies but as the lifespan of this game goes on they've fallen more and more into the trap of \"You must follow the most optimal build strats or accept defeat\" \n\nIt's boring and at the end of the day every player should just optimize to follow the same build style as the top players. It's gone beyond just having a Meta, they actively try to kill strats that do not fit their vision and so everyone must assimilate.\n\nDon't even get me started on the predatory monetization scheme that is just gambling and how you should have at minimum 4 alternate accounts to fund your main. Yeah the devs need to eat, but it's gotten to be a bit much, most of the best characters are locked behind paywalls now too. \n\nThese devs seriously lost the plot and high key suck at their jobs, I wish them the worst.",
